    "description": "Primary duties included working in a LAMP (Linux Apache MySQL PHP) stack implementing and maintaining instances of the Drupal CMS for multiple college campuses. Developed, installed, and configured third party modules to allow staff to manage content.\n\nInstalled and administered instances of Apache and MySQL for both development and production environments. Managed backup scripts, configurations, and permissions as needed.\n\nMaintained codebase/source code in the Git version control system. Used to deploy code from local development to staging/testing, and then to production servers.\n\nWorked with content editors to plan and implement new features in the CMS.\n\nResponsible for keeping up-to-date on security vulnerabilities and applying patches to servers and CMS as soon as possible.\n\nImplemented opcode (APC) and memory object caching systems (Memcached) to optimize site performance.\n\nResponsible for ensuring that pages were in compliance with Section 508 accessibility guidelines.",
